    "evidence_text": "Risingson\n\n\"Risingson\" is a song by the British trip hop group Massive Attack, released as a single on 7 July 1997.\n\n It is the first single from their third album \"Mezzanine\" and the eighth single overall.\n\nNeil Davidge (born 1962, in Bristol, UK) is a record producer, songwriter, film score composer, musician, and occasional backing vocalist.\n\n Once an associate of dance producers DNA, he is best known as the long-term co-writer and producer for the music production outfit Massive Attack.\n\nBullet Boy (soundtrack)\n\nBullet Boy by Robert Del Naja and Neil Davidge of Massive Attack is the soundtrack to the film, directed by Saul Dibb.\n\nMassive Attack (song)\n\n100th Window is the fourth studio album by English trip-hop group Massive Attack.\n\n This album marks the first studio album of Neil Davidge, after several years working as a film score composer and record producer, best known as Massive Attack's producer.\n\n The song was written by Neil Davidge and Robert Del Naja, the latter of whom performs vocals on the song.\n\n It was the first album to be produced by Neil Davidge, along with the group.",
